# Copy this file to .env and fill in your key. .env is gitignored — never commit it.
# Get a key at https://aistudio.google.com/apikey
#
# WHAT THIS KEY DOES WITH THE DOCUMENTS: with the default provider, the full text of
# every document analysed is sent over the internet to Google's Gemini API to be read.
# This tool stores nothing and logs no document text, but what Google does with it is
# outside our control, and the data-retention terms of this API tier have not been
# reviewed by us. Strip names, dates of birth, BSN and addresses out of a document
# before analysing it — no check reads them. Set CTF_PROVIDER=ollama (below) to read
# the documents on this machine and send nothing. See ETHICS.md, risk 7.

GEMINI_API_KEY=your-key-here

# --- Pooling keys ----------------------------------------------------------
# Optional. The free tier meters requests *per key, per model, per day* (about 20
# on the newest model), so a second key is a second full allowance rather than a
# faster one. Four friends' keys make five.
#
# This helps with 429 RESOURCE_EXHAUSTED and nothing else. It does NOT help with
# 503 "high demand": that is Google's shared serving capacity and every key sees
# the same outage at the same moment. The tool switches key on a 429 and switches
# model on a 503, for exactly that reason.
#
# Each of these is someone's personal credential. Treat the .env as shared secret
# material: it stays gitignored, and a key is never logged or written into a report.
# GEMINI_API_KEY_2=
# GEMINI_API_KEY_3=
# GEMINI_API_KEY_4=
# GEMINI_API_KEY_5=

# Or all at once, comma-separated. Slots 2..9 are read either way.
# GEMINI_API_KEYS=key-one,key-two,key-three

# --- Models ----------------------------------------------------------------
# CTF_MODEL=gemini-3.8-flash
# CTF_MODEL_REASONING=gemini-3.8-flash

# Tried in order when CTF_MODEL will not serve. A model can be listed by the API
# and still answer 503 "experiencing high demand" or hang until a 504; the first
# model that answers is reused for the rest of the run. The `-lite` ids are last
# on purpose — a run that ends up on one is reported as lower confidence.
# CTF_MODEL_FALLBACKS=gemini-3.7-flash,gemini-3.6-flash,gemini-3.5-flash,gemini-3-flash-preview,gemini-3.5-flash-lite,gemini-3.1-flash-lite

# --- Timing ----------------------------------------------------------------
# Seconds before one request is abandoned. This is sent to Google as the request
# deadline, not just enforced locally, so setting it too low makes the API return
# 504 DEADLINE_EXCEEDED on a model that was working fine — which then looks like an
# outage and pushes the run onto a weaker model. Measured: a 10s deadline 504s a
# healthy flash-lite after 8.7s. The API rejects anything below 10s outright.
# CTF_TIMEOUT=120

# --- Safety ----------------------------------------------------------------
# CTF_GROUNDING_MIN_RATIO=0.90
# CTF_CONFIDENCE_GATE=0.55
# Confidence multiplier applied when only a `-lite` model was available.
# CTF_DEGRADED_FACTOR=0.8

# --- Which backend reads the documents -------------------------------------
# `gemini` (the default) sends the documents to Google's API. `ollama` runs a model
# on this machine and sends nothing anywhere. Both are selectable in the UI sidebar
# and with `--provider` on the CLI; this is only the default they start on.
# CTF_PROVIDER=gemini

# --- Local models (Ollama) -------------------------------------------------
# Only used when the provider is `ollama`. Install Ollama from ollama.com, then
# `ollama pull qwen3:8b`. See the "Running it locally" section of the README for
# which model to choose.
#
# OLLAMA_HOST is Ollama's own variable and is usually already set. It is read in
# whatever form it is in: `0.0.0.0:11434` is normalised to a dialable URL.
# OLLAMA_HOST=http://localhost:11434
# CTF_OLLAMA_MODEL=qwen3:8b
# Optional. A second, larger model for the two reasoning steps, when the machine can
# hold one but not run it for everything. Defaults to CTF_OLLAMA_MODEL.
# CTF_OLLAMA_MODEL_REASONING=

# Context window in tokens, and the ceiling it may be raised to for a long bundle.
# This matters more than it looks: Ollama does not reject a prompt that overruns the
# window, it drops the front of it, and the front of these prompts is the contract.
# The client sizes each request and refuses rather than send a truncated document —
# if you hit that refusal, either raise the ceiling or lower CTF_MAX_CHARS_PER_DOC.
# Each 8k of context costs VRAM on top of the weights.
# CTF_OLLAMA_NUM_CTX=16384
# CTF_OLLAMA_MAX_CTX=32768

# Seconds before one local request is abandoned. Nothing is metered here, so this is
# generous on purpose: a model that does not fit in VRAM is slow, not broken.
# CTF_OLLAMA_TIMEOUT=600

# How long Ollama keeps the weights loaded between the pipeline's calls.
# CTF_OLLAMA_KEEP_ALIVE=10m

# `auto` (default) sends no thinking parameter, which is the only setting that works
# on both thinking and non-thinking models. `off`/`on` force it.
# CTF_OLLAMA_THINK=auto

# Local models someone has actually checked against samples/. Anything not named
# here is reported as a degraded run: confidence scaled by CTF_DEGRADED_FACTOR and a
# note in the report saying which model wrote it. Empty on purpose — see ETHICS.md.
# CTF_OLLAMA_TRUSTED=
